      "ticket_number": "FMC-2026-1289",
      "title": "\"The library system faces challenges in maintaining balanced book distribution among its branches, causing some branches to experience book shortages while others have underutilized inventory.\"",
      "description": "In college campuses, infrastructure-related problems such as damaged classroom equipment, electrical faults, water leakage, poor sanitation, Wi-Fi connectivity issues, and maintenance problems are often reported through informal communication or verbally to campus authorities. This makes it difficult to track complaints, prioritize urgent issues, assign maintenance personnel, and ensure timely resolution. Students and faculty often lack transparency regarding the progress of their reported problems, while administrators face challenges in managing multiple complaints efficiently.",
